- content_for(:title) { "Emotes — Plural Profiles" }

.card
  .card__header
    %h1 Emotes
  .admin-emotes__intro
    %p
      An emote's name sets its order in its group: #{tag.code("02_spring_heart")} comes before #{tag.code("03_hunter_heart")}.
      The code people type drops that number, so #{tag.code("02_spring_heart")} is typed as #{tag.code(":spring_heart:")}
      (typing the full name works too). Names that are all number, like #{tag.code("100")}, keep it.
    %p
      Renaming an emote keeps its old code working, so nothing already written breaks.
      Archiving hides an emote from pickers but keeps it showing wherever it's already used.

%section.card#emote-groups{"aria-labelledby": "emote-groups-heading"}
  .card__header
    %h2#emote-groups-heading Groups
  %p.admin-emotes__hint
    Groups are shown as sections in every emote picker, in this order. The symbol stands in for the group's emotes where images can't be shown, such as page titles.
  = render "admin/emotes/groups"

%section.card{"aria-labelledby": "emote-list-heading", data: { controller: "emote-filter preserve-focus" }}
  .card__header
    %h2#emote-list-heading All emotes
  .admin-emotes__toolbar
    %label.admin-emotes__filter
      %span Filter
      %input{type: "search", placeholder: "Name or code", autocomplete: "off", data: { "emote-filter-target": "input", action: "input->emote-filter#filter" }}
    %p#emote-status.admin-emotes__status{role: "status"}
  = render "admin/emotes/sections"
